ions are unseen; predictions must generalise from gene-level features and from observed perturbation effects, not from memorised labels.\\\",\\n        \\\"Control mean must be estimated from the provided control cells only; no external screen data may be used.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"evaluation_criteria\\\": [\\n        \\\"pearson_delta: per-perturbation Pearson correlation between predicted and true change-from-control vectors; rewards correct direction and relative magnitude of gene-level shifts.\\\",\\n        \\\"MSE: mean squared error of predicted vs true mean expression (or delta) across genes and perturbations; penalises scale and baseline errors.\\\",\\n        \\\"Top-20 DE metrics (MSE/PCC/R2): correctness of the strongest differentially expressed genes, which carry most biological signal.\\\",\\n        \\\"Biological validity: predicted target-gene knockdown, enrichment of known K562/CRISPRi regulon members, and consistency with essential-gene and pathway annotations.\\\",\\n        \\\"Reproducibility: deterministic pipeline, fixed seeds, documented preprocessing, and stable predictions under resampling.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"success_metrics\\\": [\\n        \\\"Mean pearson_delta across held-out perturbations substantially above zero and above a control-mean baseline.\\\",\\n        \\\"MSE lower than the variance of true perturbation means around control mean.\\\",\\n        \\\"Top-20 DE PCC and R2 above baseline and consistent with known K562 biology.\\\",\\n        \\\"Correct sign and magnitude of knockdown for the CRISPRi target gene where it is expressed.\\\",\\n        \\\"Stable rankings of top predicted DE genes across bootstrap resamples of training cells.\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \\\"key_variables\\\": {\\n      \\\"biological\\\": [\\n        \\\"Perturbation identity (CRISPRi target gene) and its baseline expression in K562.\\\",\\n        \\\"Gene-gene regulatory relationships (transcription factor targets, co-expression modules, protein complexes).\\\",\\n        \\\"Cell-state heterogeneity in K562 (cell cycle, copy-number variation, differentiation state).\\\",\\n        \\\"Essentiality and network centrality of the target gene.\\\",\\n        \\\"Baseline control expression mean and variance per gene.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"technical\\\": [\\n        \\\"Library size and CP10K normalisation, log1p transform.\\\",\\n        \\\"Guide RNA efficiency and CRISPRi knockdown strength (unobserved per perturbation).\\\",\\n        \\\"Batch/experiment effects and donor/ replicate structure in obs.\\\",\\n        \\\"Gene filtering and var order in the AnnData.\\\",\\n        \\\"Number of cells per observed perturbation (uneven support).\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"relationships\\\": [\\n        \\\"Delta_pert = f(target gene features, network neighbourhood, control expression).\\\",\\n        \\\"Perturbations targeting genes in the same complex/module produce correlated deltas.\\\",\\n        \\\"Effect magnitude scales with target expression and network centrality.\\\",\\n        \\\"Gene-level deltas are approximately additive in log space for weak perturbations.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"constraints\\\": [\\n        \\\"No held-out perturbation cells may be used at any stage, including feature construction.\\\",\\n        \\\"Control mean must be computed from control cells in the provided file.\\\",\\n        \\\"Predictions must be finite, non-negative after inverse transform considerations, and on log1p CP10K scale.\\\",\\n        \\\"Computational budget must allow full training on the provided AnnData without external downloads.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"validation_requirements\\\": [\\n        \\\"Held-out-perturbation cross-validation within the training file (simulate unseen perturbations by leaving out entire perturbation labels).\\\",\\n        \\\"Baseline comparisons: control mean, target-only knockdown, and simple linear models.\\\",\\n        \\\"Bootstrap stability of top-20 DE gene predictions.\\\",\\n        \\\"Biological sanity checks against known K562 CRISPRi hits and pathway annotations.\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \\\"scope\\\": {\\n      \\\"biological_scope\\\": \\\"Unseen-perturbation prediction of mean transcriptional response to CRISPRi knockdown in a single cancer cell line (K562). Focus on gene-level mean shifts, not cell-state distributions or guide-level heterogeneity.\\\",\\n      \\\"technical_scope\\\": \\\"Train only on cellforge_input.h5ad; build gene and perturbation feature representations from training data; predict held-out perturbation mean vectors; output predictions.npz in the required format.\\\",\\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n        \\\"Cannot model guide-specific knockdown efficiency for unseen perturbations.\\\",\\n        \\\"Cannot capture perturbation-specific cell-state composition changes beyond mean effects.\\\",\\n        \\\"Limited by the coverage and quality of observed perturbations in the training file.\\\",\\n        \\\"No external screen or literature-derived effect sizes may be used.\\\",\\n        \\\"Linear/additive assumptions may miss strong non-linear or synthetic interactions.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Control cells in the file are representative of the unperturbed K562 baseline.\\\",\\n        \\\"Gene order and normalisation are consistent between training and evaluation.\\\",\\n        \\\"Held-out perturbations share biological context (K562, CRISPRi) with training perturbations.\\\",\\n        \\\"Mean delta is the primary quantity of interest; higher moments are not scored.\\\",\\n        \\\"Gene features derived from training expression and co-expression are transferable to unseen perturbations.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"biological_validation\\\": \\\"Validate predicted deltas against known K562 CRISPRi biology: target-gene knockdown, enrichment of regulon members, essential-gene effects, and concordance with co-perturbation clusters. Use held-out-perturbation cross-validation as the primary internal proxy for the official evaluator.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"key_challenges\\\": {\\n    \\\"biological\\\": {\\n      \\\"challenges\\\": [\\n        \\\"Unseen perturbations have no cells, so no direct supervision of their effects.\\\",\\n        \\\"CRISPRi knockdown strength varies by target and guide and is unobserved.\\\",\\n        \\\"K562 has strong copy-number heterogeneity and cell-cycle structure that confound mean effects.\\\",\\n        \\\"Perturbation effects can be non-linear and context-dependent (e.g., essential genes).\\\",\\n        \\\"Many perturbations have weak or near-zero transcriptional effects, making delta prediction noisy.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Naive models collapse to control mean and yield near-zero pearson_delta; over-predicting large effects harms MSE and top-20 metrics.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": [\\n        \\\"Use gene-level features (expression, co-expression, network centrality, essentiality proxies) to transfer information to unseen targets.\\\",\\n        \\\"Shrink predicted deltas toward zero with regularisation tuned by held-out-perturbation CV.\\\",\\n        \\\"Model effect magnitude as a function of target expression and network degree.\\\",\\n        \\\"Use robust control mean estimation and per-gene variance weighting.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"validation\\\": \\\"Leave-one-perturbation-out CV on observed perturbations, stratified by effect size, with pearson_delta and top-20 metrics computed identically to the official evaluator.\\\",\\n      \\\"biological_considerations\\\": \\\"Preserve the biology that CRISPRi primarily represses the target and its regulon; enforce non-positive direct-target effects where appropriate and allow downstream positive/negative changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"technical\\\": {\\n      \\\"challenges\\\": [\\n        \\\"High-dimensional output (n_genes per perturbation) with l