th var order requirements (keep full gene set for output).\\\",\\n        \\\"Robust control mean via trimmed mean or median-of-means.\\\",\\n        \\\"Weight genes by detection rate and variance in loss/metrics.\\\",\\n        \\\"Batch-aware feature construction or batch as covariate in regression.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"validation\\\": \\\"Compare control mean estimates across batches and QC thresholds; bootstrap stability of gene features and predictions.\\\",\\n      \\\"biological_validation\\\": \\\"Check that top expressed genes and control mean match expected K562 markers (e.g., haemoglobin genes, BCR-ABL programme).\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"computational\\\": {\\n      \\\"challenges\\\": [\\n        \\\"Full gene set output requires predicting thousands of genes per perturbation.\\\",\\n        \\\"Cross-validation over perturbations multiplies training cost.\\\",\\n        \\\"Memory for dense cell x gene matrices and delta matrices.\\\",\\n        \\\"Hyperparameter tuning under strict no-leakage constraints.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Long runtimes and risk of leakage if tuning uses held-out perturbations improperly.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": [\\n        \\\"Work in reduced gene space (PCA/modules) for modelling and project back to full gene space.\\\",\\n        \\\"Use efficient linear algebra (ridge regression, SVD) and sparse representations where possible.\\\",\\n        \\\"Nested CV: inner loop for hyperparameters, outer loop for evaluation.\\\",\\n        \\\"Cache control mean and feature matrices.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"validation\\\": \\\"Profile runtime and memory; verify no held-out perturbation cells enter any fit.\\\",\\n      \\\"resource_requirements\\\": \\\"Single workstation with >=32 GB RAM, multi-core CPU; optional GPU not required; total runtime target under a few hours.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"interpretability\\\": {\\n      \\\"requirements\\\": [\\n        \\\"Predicted deltas should be attributable to target-gene features and network neighbourhood.\\\",\\n        \\\"Top-20 DE genes should be biologically plausible for each perturbation.\\\",\\n        \\\"Model should expose gene-module loadings and perturbation feature importances.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"challenges\\\": [\\n        \\\"Low-rank models can be opaque.\\\",\\n        \\\"Unseen perturbations lack direct validation of mechanism.\\\",\\n        \\\"Separating direct target knockdown from downstream effects.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"solutions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Use linear models with gene-module loadings and perturbation feature coefficients.\\\",\\n        \\\"Report per-perturbation top modules and enriched pathways.\\\",\\n        \\\"Explicitly model target-gene self-knockdown as a feature.\\\",\\n        \\\"Post-hoc enrichment analysis of predicted DE genes.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"validation\\\": \\\"Check that predicted target knockdown appears for expressed targets and that top modules match known regulons.\\\",\\n      \\\"biological_validation\\\": \\\"Compare predicted DE gene sets with known K562 CRISPRi hits and pathway annotations; verify coherence of co-perturbation clusters.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"research_questions\\\": {\\n    \\\"primary\\\": {\\n      \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Can gene-level features and observed perturbation effects in K562 CRISPRi data predict the mean transcriptional response of entirely unseen perturbations?\\\",\\n        \\\"Which feature representation (expression, co-expression modules, network centrality, essentiality proxies) best transfers to unseen CRISPRi targets?\\\",\\n        \\\"How much shrinkage toward control mean is optimal for maximising pearson_delta while controlling MSE and top-20 DE errors?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"hypotheses\\\": [\\n        \\\"A regularised low-rank model mapping perturbation features to delta vectors outperforms control-mean and target-only baselines on unseen perturbations.\\\",\\n   