nce.\\\",\\n        \\\"decision_support_quality_validation\\\": \\\"The empty decision support blocks provide no guidance on quality validation. The analysis should state that quality validation must be reconciled with the eventual evaluation strategy and risk assessment.\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"problem\\\": {\\n    \\\"definition\\\": {\\n      \\\"scope\\\": {\\n        \\\"assessment\\\": \\\"The problem scope is well defined: unseen-perturbation prediction of mean transcriptional response to CRISPRi knockdown in K562, with explicit acknowledgment that predictability varies by perturbation class. The scope appropriately limits the task to gene-level mean shifts and notes limitations regarding cell-state distributions.\\\",\\n        \\\"issues\\\": [\\n          \\\"The scope does not explicitly define how to handle perturbations with no measurable effect or lethal phenotypes beyond shrinkage.\\\",\\n          \\\"The analysis does not specify the expected number of held-out perturbations or their biological composition, which affects feasibility.\\\",\\n          \\\"The scope does not address whether predictions should be constrained to biologically plausible ranges (e.g., non-negative after inverse transform).\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"improvements\\\": [\\n          \\\"Explicitly define a strategy for perturbations with no measurable effect: predict near-zero delta with calibrated shrinkage and flag as lower-confidence.\\\",\\n          \\\"Specify the expected number and biological composition of held-out perturbations (if known) to set feasibility expectations.\\\",\\n          \\\"Add constraints on predicted values: ensure predictions are finite and on the log1p CP10k scale, and consider non-negativity after inverse transform.\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"validation\\\": \\\"Validate scope by confirming that the evaluation metrics (pearson_delta, MSE, top-20 DE metrics) are computed exactly as the evaluator does, and that the scope's