e loading coherence\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"results\\\": \\\"Not yet computed; evaluator is Gene-Mila's external scorer. No results are available in the provided metadata.\\\",\\n        \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"pearson_delta rewards correct direction and relative magnitude of transcriptional change; top-20 metrics reward recovery of the strongest biological effects. A model that predicts control mean for all perturbations will score near zero on pearson_delta and poorly on top-20 metrics. For perturbations with no measurable transcriptional effect, predict near-zero delta with calibrated shrinkage and flag as lower-confidence; report stratified performance by target-gene class. Calibrated shrinkage procedure: shrink predicted deltas by a factor alpha in [0,1] tuned via leave-one-perturbation-out CV to maximize pearson_delta subject to an MSE constraint, with alpha stratified by target-gene class and neighbor distance.\\\",\\n        \\\"decision_support_validation\\\": \\\"No validation plan is supplied in the empty decision-support blocks; the evaluator's metrics should be mirrored in an internal held-out split of training perturbations to select model and hyperparameters before final prediction. Use nested cross-validation (inner loop for hyperparameters, outer loop for evaluation) to avoid leakage during tuning. Biological relevance criteria (required target knockdown sign, pathway enrichment thresholds) must be defined once decision support is populated. Interpretability claims should be validated against known K562 CRISPRi biology and reported as secondary validation, not used for model selection.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"technical\\\": {\\n        \\\"methods\\\": [\\n          \\\"Held-out split within training perturbations (perturbation-level cross-validation)\\\",\\n          \\\"Inspection of guide-assignment confidence and cell-level QC\\\",\\n          \\\"Reproducibility check of normalization (CP10k + log1p) via max value and non-integer 